      "cwe_id": "CWE-639",
      "explanation": "The endpoint `user_orders` allows any authenticated user to retrieve the orders of any other user by specifying their `user_id`. There is no check to ensure that the requesting user is the owner of the orders or an administrator. This is a classic Insecure Direct Object Reference (IDOR) vulnerability.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "type": "code",
          "file": "app/routes/users.py",
          "lines": [
            56,
            62
          ],
          "source": null,
          "content": "@users_bp.route(\"/<int:user_id>/orders\", methods=[\"GET\"])\n@require_auth\ndef user_orders(user_id: int):\n    \"\"\"List a user's orders.\"\"\"\n    session = get_session()\n    orders = session.query(Order).filter(Order.user_id == user_id).all()\n    return jsonify([o.to_dict() for o in orders])",
          "snapshot": null,
          "snapshot_conflict": false,
          "grounded_in_pr": true
        }
      ],
      "suggested_fix": "Add an authorization check to ensure the current user is either the owner of the orders or an administrator. For example: `if not is_owner_or_admin(g.current_user.id, user_id): abort(403)`.",
